  "interpretation": [
    "The remaining-mass check detects both the actual 921 exception and a positive neighbor accepted by the original solver. The seven-step lookback of 72,967 constrained rows is specific to this signature and does not estimate a campaign-wide frequency.",
    "A check guarded by solve misses incorrectly skipped rows. Compensating the preliminary totals corrects two constructed rows on both backends but rejects a legitimate capacity-limited case with k=2 and cap sum 1+2^-26.",
    "Even with an independent unit budget, a real interior of 1-2^-26 rounds to the stored cap 1. Correctly rounded values can have a nonzero compensated sum residual, and the face used for the VJP can differ from the stored face.",
    "Preserve the origin and roundoff of chosen total bounds and the mathematical active face through storage. Treat ambiguous rows as candidates for local reconstruction and certify against representability and boundary conditions. Cross-check values, weak support, and VJPs with exact small-row references.",
    "Only terminal-check healthy-update cost was measured end to end; the NPU runs used the CPU checkpoint's portable state with a fixed device seed. Repeated NPU baseline updates also produced distinct gradient digests. The observed times do not qualify a repaired release or estimate the whole matrix."
  ],
  "mechanism": {
    "complexity": "For k candidates the new ordinary comparisons need O(k) work per row in addition to existing O(k log k) sorting. Refinement revisits the remaining candidates for at most k+1 passes, O(k^2) work per selected row and O(k) temporary storage. An original FP32 bisection uses 40 iterations and may execute tensor operations over the slab.",
    "entry_test": "Also use compensated sums before deciding on activation and before selecting the aggregate box endpoints. The test still receives the rounded scalar totals constructed by allocate().",
    "ordinary": "Solve the active fixed total when it lies strictly between aggregate bounds; use sorted breakpoints, face bounds and the existing safeguarded bisection if needed.",
    "refinement": "Re-center original scores among free coordinates; peg coordinates provably saturated according to the sign of the clipped residual; redistribute the remaining mass. Refine only selected rows in the same device dtype.",
    "source_diffs": {
      "entry_and_terminal_check": {
        "lines_added": 73,
